## const — rebinding protection only

```js
const user = { name: 'Aaron', age: 30 };

user.age = 31;        // ✅ mutation — fine with const
user.role = 'admin';  // ✅ adding a property — also fine

user = { name: 'Bob' }; // ❌ TypeError: Assignment to constant variable
```

## Object.freeze() — shallow property lock

```js
const config = Object.freeze({
  host: 'localhost',
  port: 3000,
  db: { name: 'mydb' },
});

config.port = 8080;      // ❌ silently ignored (or throws in strict mode)
config.extra = 'nope';   // ❌ also ignored
console.log(config.port); // still 3000

// BUT nested objects are NOT frozen:
config.db.name = 'hacked'; // ✅ mutation succeeds!
```

## Deep freeze

```js
function deepFreeze(obj) {
  Object.getOwnPropertyNames(obj).forEach(name => {
    const value = obj[name];
    if (value && typeof value === 'object') deepFreeze(value);
  });
  return Object.freeze(obj);
}

const frozen = deepFreeze({ a: { b: { c: 42 } } });
frozen.a.b.c = 99; // silently fails — fully frozen
```

## Summary

| | `const` | `Object.freeze()` |
|---|---|---|
| Prevents reassignment | ✅ | ❌ |
| Prevents property mutation | ❌ | ✅ (shallow) |
| Affects nested objects | ❌ | ❌ (shallow) |
| Runtime enforcement | ✅ | ✅ |

